        "#6. Temperature Classifier\n",
        "Create a Python program that asks the user to input a temperature in Celsius. Based on the\n",
        "temperature value, print whether it's 'Freezing' (below 0°C), 'Cold' (0-10°C), 'Moderate'\n",
        "(11-25°C), 'Warm' (26-30°C), or 'Hot' (above 30°C)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6Cr0KtCO_9Sx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "temp=int(input(\"Enter temperature(in celsius): \"))\n",
        "if temp<0:\n",
        "  print(\"Freezing\")\n",
        "elif 0<=temp<=10:\n",
        "  print(\"Cold\")\n",
        "elif 10<temp<=25:\n",
        "  print(\"Moderate\")\n",
        "elif 25<temp<=30:\n",
        "  print(\"Warm\")\n",
        "else:\n",
        "  print(\"Hot\")\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
